The value of N_{\\rm H} is well within the range derived from observations of the source with the _XMM-Newton_, _Chandra_, and _Swift_ observatories (e.g., Campana et al., 2014). N_{\\rm H} measurements from radio and infrared maps of Galactic hydrogen1(Schlegel et al., 1998; Kalberla et al., 2005; Willingale et al., 2013) find within 1^{\\circ} of the source N_{\\rm H}=4.30\\times 10^{21} cm{}^{-2}, which is 20% lower than our value. Because the difference is modest, we use our value in the burst analysis for consistency.

